.\" sharedwatch(1) — manual page
.\" Install: cp man/sharedwatch.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/ && sudo mandb
.\" View:    man sharedwatch
.\"
.\" Source of truth for the program: src/cmd/sharedwatch/main.go
.\" When commands or flags change, update this file in the same PR.
.TH SHAREDWATCH 1 "2026-05-24" "v0.0.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sharedwatch \- calm, pull-based activity journal for a local shared folder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sharedwatch
[\fIglobal flags\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIcommand flags\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sharedwatch
is a single Go binary that watches one or more folders on disk and writes
every observed change into a durable, SQLite-backed event journal. A separate
consumer runs on its own cadence (passive every 10 min by default, active
every 5 s) and turns batches of events into reviewable digests.
.PP
The watcher and consumer never communicate directly \(em they share one DB.
The watcher writes events; the consumer pulls. A reconcile loop runs every
30 min as a safety net to catch anything the watcher missed.
.PP
Multiple folders can be watched by one daemon with stable labels
(\fB--root\fR \fIlabel\fR=\fIpath\fR). Every event carries a
\fBpayload_json\fR v1 envelope with optional \fBactor\fR, \fBsession\fR,
\fBtask\fR, \fBintent\fR, \fBaddressee\fR, \fBref_event_id\fR, and \fBtags\fR
fields for multi-writer coordination.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create the data dir and DB; print the resolved paths.
.TP
.B run
Start the watcher + consumer + reconcile loop. One per data dir; a file
lock at \fI<data_dir>/sharedwatch.lock\fR prevents two daemons racing.
.TP
.B status \fR[\fB--json\fR] [\fB--actors\fR]
Print current mode, queue depth, last consumer/reconcile run.
With \fB--actors\fR includes the actors registry.
.TP
.B roots \fR[\fB--json\fR]
List the folders being watched. Works for both single and multi-root setups.
The default (\fIsingle-root\fR) entry has an empty label and points at
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/sharedwatch/watch\fR unless overridden.
.TP
.B mode active \fR[\fB--ttl\fR \fIduration\fR]
Enable active mode (consumer runs every 5 s) for the given TTL. Each
successful consume extends the TTL.
.TP
.B mode passive
Force passive mode (consumer runs every 10 min).
.TP
.B consume
Process pending events once and create a digest. Useful for cron-driven
external schedulers.
.TP
.B digest list \fR[\fB--limit\fR \fIN\fR]
List recent digests, newest first.
.TP
.B digest show \fIid\fR
Print one digest in full and mark it read.
.TP
.B digest archive \fIid\fR
Mark a digest archived.
.TP
.B reconcile now
Run the reconcile pass immediately.
.TP
.B events list \fR[\fIflags\fR]
Read-only query against the events table. Flags include \fB--since\fR
(RFC3339 timestamp or duration like \fI5m\fR), \fB--type\fR, \fB--source\fR,
\fB--status\fR, \fB--producer\fR, \fB--path-glob\fR, \fB--limit\fR,
\fB--order\fR (asc|desc), \fB--format\fR (text|json|jsonl|csv),
\fB--fields\fR (comma-separated projection), \fB--since-cursor\fR (stateless
token), \fB--cursor-name\fR (server-side named cursor that advances on read),
\fB--no-advance\fR, \fB--payload-key\fR/\fB--payload-value\fR (post-fetch
filter), and \fB--root\fR (filter by watch-root label).
.TP
.B events stats \fR\fB--root\fR \fIlabel\fR
Per-root aggregate counts. Required scope (one root) keeps the response
bounded and forces agents to choose the dimension before drilling.
.TP
.B events cursor list|reset \fIname\fR|set \fIname\fR|encode|decode
Manage server-side iteration cursors.
.TP
.B events retry \fR[\fB--max-retries\fR \fIN\fR]
Requeue failed events back to pending.
.TP
.B events recover-stuck \fR[\fB--older-than\fR \fIduration\fR]
Flip events stuck in 'processing' state back to pending. Default cutoff 5m.
.TP
.B overview \fR[\fB--format\fR text|json] [\fB--since\fR \fIduration\fR]
Cross-root L1 summary with by-type counts, top actors, and a \fIdrill\fR map
of pre-computed follow-up commands.
.TP
.B sql \fIstmt\fR|-|\fB--file\fR \fIpath\fR \fR[\fB--write\fR] [\fB--format\fR text|json|jsonl|csv]
Run a SQL query. SELECT/WITH/EXPLAIN/PRAGMA table_info only by default.
\fB--write\fR allows mutations \(em a tripwire, not a security boundary.
.TP
.B schema \fR[\fItable\fR] [\fB--format\fR text|json]
Print live DDL from the DB.
.TP
.B actor heartbeat \fIactor-id\fR \fR[\fB--focus\fR \fIglob\fR] [\fB--kind\fR \fIk\fR] [\fB--label\fR \fIl\fR] [\fB--metadata\fR \fIjson\fR]
Register or heartbeat an actor in the actors registry.
.TP
.B intent declare \fIpath\fR \fB--actor\fR \fIid\fR \fR[\fB--ttl\fR \fId\fR] [\fB--intent\fR \fItext\fR]
Cooperative intent declaration on a path. Peer agents SHOULD respect it.
.TP
.B lease acquire \fIpath-glob\fR \fB--actor\fR \fIid\fR \fR[\fB--ttl\fR \fId\fR]
Acquire an advisory lease on a path-glob. The watcher logs a warning when
another actor writes to the locked area.
.TP
.B test emit \fR[\fIrelpath\fR] [\fB--payload\fR \fIjson\fR | attribution flags]
Inject a synthetic event for end-to-end testing. The \fB--payload\fR raw
JSON form and the attribution flags (\fB--actor\fR \fIetc\fR) are mutually
exclusive.
.TP
.B update \fR[\fB--apply\fR] [\fB--version\fR \fItag\fR] [\fB--repo\fR \fIowner/repo\fR] [\fB--yes\fR] [\fB--timeout\fR \fIduration\fR]
Check for or install a newer release. Dry-run by default. With
\fB--apply\fR: downloads the tarball + manifest.yaml from
\fIraw.githubusercontent.com\fR, SHA-256 verifies, smoke-tests the new
binary, then atomic-renames it over the current path. Refuses if the
binary's parent directory isn't writable by the current user (no sudo
escalation). Safe to run while a daemon is active.
.TP
.B version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B help
Print the embedded help.
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
.TP
.BR --config " " \fIpath\fR
Config file (default \fIconfig.yaml\fR; silently ignored if missing).
.TP
.BR --watch-path " " \fIdir\fR
Override the single watch path. Repeatable (comma-aware) for multi-root.
Use \fB--root\fR for explicitly labelled multi-root setups.
.TP
.BR --root " " \fIlabel\fR=\fIpath\fR
Register a watch root (definition only on the root flagset). With just
\fIlabel\fR (no \fI=path\fR) on a subcommand flagset, filters by that root.
Repeatable.
.TP
.BR --db " " \fIfile\fR
Override the SQLite DB path.
.TP
.BR --data-dir " " \fIdir\fR
Override the data directory.
.TP
.BR --ignore " " \fIpattern\fR
Extra ignore pattern. Repeatable, comma-aware. Appended to the default list.
.TP
.BR --include " " \fIpattern\fR
Include-only filter, applied before ignores. Repeatable, comma-aware.
Empty (default) means include all.
.TP
.BR --hash " " on|off
Enable per-file SHA-256 content hashing during snapshot building. Default off.
.TP
.BR --producer " " \fIid\fR
Override the \fBproducer_id\fR stamped on emitted events. Default
\fI<host>:<pid>\fR.
.TP
.BR --log-format " " text|json
Log format. Default \fItext\fR.
.TP
.BR --log-level " " debug|info|warn|error
Log level. Default \fIinfo\fR.
.TP
.BR --hints " " default|agent|terse|off
Next-step suggestions profile. \fIdefault\fR shows up to 4 contextual
hints in human output; \fIagent\fR shows up to 8 hints designed for AI
agents reading the JSON envelope; \fIterse\fR shows at most 1 hint
without a reason line; \fIoff\fR suppresses entirely. Resolution order:
flag > env (\fBSHAREDWATCH_HINTS\fR) > auto-promote to \fIagent\fR for
\fB--format json\fR > \fIdefault\fR.
.TP
.BR --version
Same as the \fBversion\fR subcommand.
.SH ATTRIBUTION FLAGS
Available on the root flagset (apply to every event the daemon emits during
this lifetime) and on \fBtest emit\fR (override per-event). Populate the
\fBpayload_json\fR v1 envelope.
.TP
.BR --actor " " \fIid\fR
Stable id of the writer. Required to use any other attribution flag.
.TP
.BR --actor-kind " " human|ai_agent|automation
Kind of writer.
.TP
.BR --session " " \fIid\fR
Logical-run identifier; convention \fIsess-YYYY-MM-DD-<short>\fR.
.TP
.BR --task " " \fIlabel\fR
Short human-meaningful work label.
.TP
.BR --intent " " \fItext\fR
One-sentence reason.
.TP
.BR --addressee " " \fIid\fR
Who the change is FOR (peer agent or human).
.TP
.BR --ref " " \fIevent-id\fR
Causal predecessor event id (sets \fBref_event_id\fR).
.TP
.BR --tag " " \fItag\fR
Repeatable, comma-aware. Sets \fBpayload_json.tags[]\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
First-time setup:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sharedwatch init
sharedwatch run &
.EE
.RE
.PP
See what is being watched:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sharedwatch roots
sharedwatch roots --json
.EE
.RE
.PP
Multi-root with labels:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sharedwatch --root auth=/work/auth --root billing=/work/billing run &
sharedwatch --root auth events list --since 1h --format jsonl
.EE
.RE
.PP
Attribute every event from this invocation:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sharedwatch --actor claude-coord --task refactor-auth \\
            --intent "split monolithic login.go" run
.EE
.RE
.PP
Incremental cursor-based read for an agent:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sharedwatch events list --cursor-name my-agent --format jsonl
.EE
.RE
.PP
Smoke test the full pipeline:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sharedwatch test emit hello.md --actor demo --task quick-smoke
sharedwatch consume
sharedwatch digest list
.EE
.RE
.PP
Keep the binary current:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sharedwatch update              # dry-run, no changes
sharedwatch update --apply      # download + SHA-256 verify + atomic swap
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/sharedwatch/watch
Default watched folder.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/sharedwatch/queue.db
Default SQLite DB. WAL mode; foreign-key cascade enabled.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/sharedwatch/sharedwatch.lock
File lock held by the active \fBrun\fR process to prevent concurrent
daemons. PID of the holder is written to the file.
.TP
.I ./config.yaml
Optional config file searched in the current working directory. Silently
ignored if missing. Override with \fB--config\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for default \fIdata_dir\fR. Defaults to
\fI$HOME/.local/share\fR when unset.
.TP
.B SHAREDWATCH_HINTS
Default profile for next-step suggestions. One of \fIdefault\fR,
\fIagent\fR, \fIterse\fR, \fIoff\fR. Overridden by the \fB--hints\fR
flag. See \fB--hints\fR under GLOBAL FLAGS for resolution rules.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Operational failure (DB error, file I/O, network error during \fBupdate\fR).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown subcommand, malformed flags).
